TITLE='Authentic title "Do This Once You Have $50,000 Saved" is a milestone-trigger promise in a channel series ($20,000 and $100,000 versions are STRONG peers). The script delivers an ordered checklist (emergency fund, match, debt, Roth IRA, 401(k), HSA, index funds, automation), so the promise is honoured.'
THUMB='Registered maxresdefault 1280x720 (HTTP 200, real image). White field. Left: the recurring cartoon man in a blue hoodie with a sly smile, holding a large gold key. Centre: black headline "50K TO 100K". Right: an open grey vault glowing yellow with a green dial, a black arrow from key to vault. At 320x180 the headline stays legible; key and vault remain identifiable. The "50K TO 100K" promise is not in the title and maps to the script\'s claim that Jaime doubled the money, which the audit finds misleading.'
SCRIPT='A single-narrator milestone checklist using two composite 30-year-olds (Alex leaves $50,000 at 0.01%, Jaime follows a framework): inaction cost and loss aversion, emergency fund in a high-yield account, employer match, high-interest debt, Roth IRA, extra 401(k), HSA, three-fund or target-date portfolio with SPIVA and the Buffett bet, behaviour gap (DALBAR, J.P. Morgan best days, Morningstar), a five-year Alex vs Jaime comparison, Munger quote, close. Most limits and arithmetic are right; the Buffett average, $500,000 match loss, $134,000 fee drag, VXUS fee and the five-year doubling are wrong or overstated.'
